    details = <
        ["de"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::de]>
            purpose = <"*To record the findings observed during the physical examination of a placenta. (en)">
            use = <"*Use to record the observed findings during the physical examination of a placenta.

This archetype has been specifically designed to be used in the 'Examination detail' SLOT within the OBSERVATION.exam, the 'Procedure detail' SLOT within the ACTION.procedure archetype, or the 'Additional details' SLOT within the EVALUATION.pregnancy_summary, but can also be used within other ENTRY or CLUSTER archetypes, where clinically appropriate. 

Interpretation of the findings, for example 'No abnormality detected' or 'Moderate inflammation present', can be recorded using the 'Clinical interpretation' data element.

Use to provide a framework in which CLUSTER archetypes can be nested in the 'Examination findings' SLOT to record additional structured physical examination findings.

The CLUSTER.exclusion_exam archetype can be nested within the 'Examination not done' SLOT to optionally record explicit details about the examination not being performed.

Use to incorporate the narrative descriptions of clinical findings within existing or legacy clinical systems into an archetyped format, using the 'Clinical Description' data element. (en)">
            misuse = <"*Not to be used for recording the results of an imaging examination - use the CLUSTER.imaging_exam family of archetypes for this purpose. (en)">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation">
        >
        ["sv"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::sv]>
            purpose = <"*To record the findings observed during the physical examination of a placenta. (en)">
            keywords = <"fynd, undersökningsfynd, fysisk undersökning, u.a., utan anmärkning", ...>
            use = <"*Use to record the observed findings during the physical examination of a placenta.

This archetype has been specifically designed to be used in the 'Examination detail' SLOT within the OBSERVATION.exam, the 'Procedure detail' SLOT within the ACTION.procedure archetype, or the 'Additional details' SLOT within the EVALUATION.pregnancy_summary, but can also be used within other ENTRY or CLUSTER archetypes, where clinically appropriate. 

Interpretation of the findings, for example 'No abnormality detected' or 'Moderate inflammation present', can be recorded using the 'Clinical interpretation' data element.

Use to provide a framework in which CLUSTER archetypes can be nested in the 'Examination findings' SLOT to record additional structured physical examination findings.

The CLUSTER.exclusion_exam archetype can be nested within the 'Examination not done' SLOT to optionally record explicit details about the examination not being performed.

Use to incorporate the narrative descriptions of clinical findings within existing or legacy clinical systems into an archetyped format, using the 'Clinical Description' data element. (en)">
            misuse = <"*Not to be used for recording the results of an imaging examination - use the CLUSTER.imaging_exam family of archetypes for this purpose. (en)">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation">
        >
        ["nb"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::nb]>
            purpose = <"For å registrere observerte funn ved fysisk undersøkelse av placenta.">
            use = <"Brukes til å registrere observerte funn ved fysisk undersøkelse av placenta. 

Arketypen er laget spesifikt for å brukes i \"Undersøkelsesdetaljer\"-SLOTet i arketypen OBSERVATION.exam, \"Prosedyredetaljer\"-SLOTet i arketypen ACTION.prosedyre eller \"Ytterligere detaljer\"-SLOTet i EVALUATION.pregnancy_summary, men kan også brukes innen andre ENTRY- og CLUSTER-arketyper der det er klinisk passende. 

Tolkning av funnene, for eksempel \"Ingen abnormitet detektert\" eller \"Moderat inflammasjon tilstede\", kan registreres ved å bruke dataelementet \"Klinisk tolkning\".

Brukes for å gi et rammeverk der CLUSTER-arketyper kan nøstes i \"Undersøkelsesfunn\"-SLOTet for å registrere ytterligere strukturerte fysiske undersøkelsesfunn. 

Arketypen CLUSTER.exclusion_exam kan nøstes i \"Undersøkelse ikke gjort\"-SLOTet for å alternativt registrere eksplisitte detaljer om undersøkelsen som ikke kan utføres. 

Brukes for å videreføre fritekstbeskrivelse av kliniske funn fra tidligere systemer inn i et arketypeformat, ved å bruke elementet \"Klinisk beskrivelse\".">
            misuse = <"Brukes ikke til å registrere resultatene av en bildeundersøkelse - bruk arketypefamilien CLUSTER.imaging_exam til dette formålet.">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation">
        >
        ["pt-br"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::pt-br]>
            purpose = <"*To record the findings observed during the physical examination of a placenta. (en)">
            use = <"*Use to record the observed findings during the physical examination of a placenta.

This archetype has been specifically designed to be used in the 'Examination detail' SLOT within the OBSERVATION.exam, the 'Procedure detail' SLOT within the ACTION.procedure archetype, or the 'Additional details' SLOT within the EVALUATION.pregnancy_summary, but can also be used within other ENTRY or CLUSTER archetypes, where clinically appropriate. 

Interpretation of the findings, for example 'No abnormality detected' or 'Moderate inflammation present', can be recorded using the 'Clinical interpretation' data element.

Use to provide a framework in which CLUSTER archetypes can be nested in the 'Examination findings' SLOT to record additional structured physical examination findings.

The CLUSTER.exclusion_exam archetype can be nested within the 'Examination not done' SLOT to optionally record explicit details about the examination not being performed.

Use to incorporate the narrative descriptions of clinical findings within existing or legacy clinical systems into an archetyped format, using the 'Clinical Description' data element. (en)">
            misuse = <"*Not to be used for recording the results of an imaging examination - use the CLUSTER.imaging_exam family of archetypes for this purpose. (en)">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation">
        >
        ["en"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::en]>
            purpose = <"To record the findings observed during the physical examination of a placenta.">
            use = <"Use to record the observed findings during the physical examination of a placenta.

This archetype has been specifically designed to be used in the 'Examination detail' SLOT within the OBSERVATION.exam, the 'Procedure detail' SLOT within the ACTION.procedure archetype, or the 'Additional details' SLOT within the EVALUATION.pregnancy_summary, but can also be used within other ENTRY or CLUSTER archetypes, where clinically appropriate. 

Interpretation of the findings, for example 'No abnormality detected' or 'Moderate inflammation present', can be recorded using the 'Clinical interpretation' data element.

Use to provide a framework in which CLUSTER archetypes can be nested in the 'Examination findings' SLOT to record additional structured physical examination findings.

The CLUSTER.exclusion_exam archetype can be nested within the 'Examination not done' SLOT to optionally record explicit details about the examination not being performed.

Use to incorporate the narrative descriptions of clinical findings within existing or legacy clinical systems into an archetyped format, using the 'Clinical Description' data element.">
            misuse = <"Not to be used for recording the results of an imaging examination - use the CLUSTER.imaging_exam family of archetypes for this purpose.">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation">
        >
    >

definition
    CLUSTER[at0000.1] matches {    -- Examination of a placenta
        items matches {
            ELEMENT[at0001.1] matches {    -- System or structure examined
                value matches {
                    DV_CODED_TEXT[at0.9000] matches {
                        defining_code matches {[at0.1]}    -- Placenta
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

